# Perf / cost lock (FROZEN 2026-09-12)

Owner mandate: **minimal RAM**, **minimal Vercel spend**, **fast on all devices**, **no freeze/jank**.
Ponytail level: **`lite`** (not full/ultra unless owner says otherwise).

## Size caps (do not commit / push / deploy over)

Enforced by `scripts/check-repo-weight.mjs` (pre-commit, pre-push `--ci`, `prebuild --ci`, `postbuild --build`). Raise only with owner approval + date bump here + matching constants in the script.

| Cap | Lock | Now |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Git tree | **96 MiB** / **3500** files | ~77 MiB / ~2800 |
| Vercel deploy (`.next/server`+`static`, no maps/cache) | **100 MiB** | ~87 MiB after map strip |
| `.next/server` (no maps) | **80 MiB** | ~71 MiB |
| `.next/static` | **24 MiB** | ~16 MiB |
| Per-file new blob | **512 KiB** (existing LARGE_OK prefixes) | — |
| Function RAM | **256 MB** default / **1024 MB** ceiling | vercel.json |
| Next start heap | **≤768 MB** | package.json `start` |
| Crons | **≤6** | vercel.json |
| SEO SSG hubs | **<80** | cdn-cache.check.ts |

Why 100 MiB deploy: Vercel uncompressed function wall is 250 MiB; maps were 136 MiB of waste; 100 MiB keeps Fluid compute + upload + cold starts cheap. Over cap = build fail = no push to Vercel.

## Client RAM / speed

| Source | Lock |
| --- | --- |
| `app/src/lib/device-budget.ts` | `LITE_BOOT` sets `data-lite` on user lock (`sv-lite`), ≤4 GB RAM, ≤4 cores, Save-Data, reduced motion |
| Map caps | `mapRuntimeOptions()`: lite tile cache 16, full 48; pixelRatio cap; no resource timing / preserveDrawingBuffer |
| Regression guard | `device-budget.check.ts` — run on change; build fails if locks break |
| Heavy UI | Dynamic import maps (`Map3DLazy`), listing `MapEmbed` lazy, lite skips reveal + GTM |
| Listing/search clients | Import `map-geo` / `map-href` — never `buildings.ts` or `geocode.ts` (footprints + streets JSON) |
| Motion | `reducedMotion="user"` in I18nProvider — never `"never"` |

## Server / Vercel

| Source | Lock |
| --- | --- |
| `app/vercel.json` | Catch-all `src/app/api/**/*` pinned **256 MB**; per-route `memory`/`maxDuration` overrides — most-specific glob wins |
| Default API routes | **Enforced** 256 MB via catch-all; >1024 MB or unpinned route fails `device-budget.check.ts` |
| Hot paths | search/map-data/ai/cron: 1024 MB max — already ceiling |
| DB pool | `src/lib/db.ts` `max: 1` — one connection per lambda |
| Runtime | Fluid Compute (Node), **not** `runtime = 'edge'` unless required |
| Region | `fra1` only unless multi-region approved |
| Sentry | `replaysSessionSampleRate: 0` |
| Source maps | `productionBrowserSourceMaps: false` + `experimental.serverSourceMaps: false`; **postbuild deletes `*.map`** (Turbopack ignores the flag today) |
| Image opt | `images.unoptimized: true` — never Vercel Image Optimization bill |
| Paid Vercel pkgs | Ban `@vercel/analytics` `@vercel/speed-insights` `@vercel/toolbar` `@vercel/otel` |
| Upload | `app/.vercelignore` drops ios/android/e2e/docs — not in the Vercel tarball |

## Agent rules (ponytail lite)

1. **Deletion over addition** — no new deps, bundles, or serverless routes without measuring need.
2. **Lazy load** heavy client chunks; SSR only what LCP needs.
3. **Cache** at CDN/ISR before adding compute; prefer static/JSON over live API.
4. **No polling** `performance.memory`; detect once via `LITE_BOOT` / `isLiteDevice()`.
5. **No background work** on main thread — ResizeObserver/debounce for map resize only.
6. Change `device-budget.ts`, `vercel.json`, or `db.ts` pool → update `device-budget.check.ts` in same PR.
7. **Never raise** `MAX_DEPLOY_BYTES` / `MAX_TRACKED_BYTES` / function `memory` without owner + date bump. Over-cap build must fail, not warn.
8. No `@vercel/analytics`, Speed Insights, Web Analytics, extra regions, extra crons, or Vercel Image Optimization.

Change locks only with explicit owner approval + date bump here.
